today we're going to tackle the mojito  one of the most popular cocktails in the  world there are a lot of different ways  to make it this is how I like to do it  with a little less soda water and really  letting the min be the star of the show  you only need a handful of ingredients  white rum mint lime soda water and  simple syrup if you don't know how  simple syrup is a cinch to make all it  takes is equal parts sugar and hot water  from the tap  stir it up dissolve it and it keeps in  the fridge for up to a month we're going  to start with an ounce of simple syrup  followed by about eight to ten minutes  and we're gonna muddle those together  when you're muddling remember not to  press too hard you don't want to  pulverize the mint or any herbs you just  want to extract those aromatic oils not  the bitter tannins in the fibers good  now we'll juice some limes remember  fresh juice always put it right into the  [ __ ] here 3/4 of an ounce and finally  2 ounces of white rum when you're  looking for a white rum to buy look for  something with a number on the label it  usually means it's been aged and then  filtered for color but it still retains  some of that rich flavor from the barrel  okay now we're ready to shake  all right strain this into a highball  glass over ice  top it off just a splash little bit of  soda  finally beautiful mint sprig for garnish  so that's how you make a mojito now  you're ready to sit back by the pool put  your feet up and enjoy this classic  Cuban cocktail if you liked this video  and you're looking for more tips to step  up your bartending game subscribe to the  GQ channel if not lots more where that  came from
 

